    University of Queensland (Australia)<br>
    <a href="{{ resource_url_9 }}">{{ resource_url_9 }}</a><br>
    Hot water was effective as glyphosate herbicide. Flaming was less effective, but acceptable weed kill was obtained on juvenile weeds.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span data-field="resource_title_10">{{ resource_title_10 }}</span><br>
    Ecological Farmers Association of Ontario<br>
    <a href="{{ resource_url_10 }}">{{ resource_url_10 }}</a><br>
    A brief report on field trials regarding flame weeding in potato production.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span data-field="resource_title_11">{{ resource_title_11 }}</span><br>
    By Sheila Daar<br>
    <a href="{{ resource_url_11 }}">{{ resource_url_11 }}</a><br>
